model {
  extend basalt {
    build = module "Build" {
      description "Each production-operation binding proof runs alone with its own database. The scope runner builds the shared framework once after installing its proof inputs, and each isolated managed run explicitly reuses that unchanged build output. CI assigns each identity scenario its own matrix job so independent Cloud startup costs do not accumulate against one job deadline. Before Vitest starts, binding variants preboot original and changed Alchemy stages with the same canonical origin and configured secrets; timed fixture operations only switch the retained listener, and suite teardown owns both runtimes. App lint reads the immutable host manifest from the exact pinned Git object in its sparse source checkout and then applies manifest carries. It needs no live content API request or host installation. The shared-account health scenario runs in the hosted account gate and identifies status dots by their image role. Physical database fixtures hold runner-owned shared table locks across the clone and both account and receipt baseline reads. The lock scope rolls back before target selection and releases on failure, so normal writes resume after the consistent baseline is captured. Managed Cloud owns a retained canonical loopback listener before creating fixtures. The production-operation database proxy also binds an OS-assigned loopback listener before allocating its backend and keeps it for the environment scope. Runtime bindings and fixture replies use that actual held port. Proxy startup and cleanup failures retain only closed OS codes and bounded errno values; raw exception messages and nested causes never enter diagnostics. Alchemy binds the private API on an OS-assigned port with bind-only collision recovery, and startup output supplies the actual forwarding destination. Deliberate restarts keep the canonical origin and replace only that destination. Managed Cloud startup retains sanitized Alchemy failure output through stream completion or a bounded quiet period before rejecting readiness. The same cause reaches cloud.log and the startup error; successful readiness has no extra wait. Compiler evidence waits on saved-line notifications through authenticated fixture control until its trace and source digest reach the requested phase, within the scenario's existing deadline. Documentation builds read licensed Latin Geist faces from repository assets through the local font provider, including normal and italic variable weight ranges. CI rebuilds with empty font caches and refuses font requests to the outside service. Live model-probe capture keeps bounded response bodies, including non-JSON failures, with credentials redacted before evidence leaves the browser. The dashboard renderer excludes browser analytics through the framework compiler's client-only boundary; browser event capture and replay keep the same synchronous entry points."
      metadata { code "scripts|.upstream/e2e|assets/fonts/geist|e2e/slack/catalog.mjs|e2e/slack/run.ts|containers/pool/fetch_releases.py|containers/pool/fetch_sources.py|containers/pool/Dockerfile|.github/workflows/ci.yml|.github/workflows/app-lint.yml|.github/workflows/client-desktop-mac.yml"; libraries "@effect/platform-node|alchemy|esbuild|fontTools.subset|fontTools.ttLib.TTFont"; bindings "platform.env.POOL_OPERATIONS=basalt.modelGateway" }
    }
  }
}
